# Normalize line endings on commit and check out LF everywhere.
#
# Why this file exists: on 2026-09-13 the deployed working tree had to be
# re-cloned because the previous one was cloned on Windows and copied to Linux.
# Every file differed by CRLF, so nothing was committable and the tree looked
# entirely modified. This is a public MIT repo — any contributor on Windows
# hits the same trap without this.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text files; `eol=lf` forces LF in the working
# tree as well as in the index, so a Windows checkout does not reintroduce CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.gguf binary
*.safetensors binary
*.bin binary
*.pt binary
*.onnx binary
